<div class="docs-hero">
  <h1>Roadmap</h1>
  <p>Flint UI's goal: a mini design system in the spirit of Material Design 2 —
     a small, opinionated set of flat, Google-flavored app shells and
     components, backed by a docs site that makes each piece copy-pasteable.</p>
</div>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="rm-principles">Guiding principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Docs ship with every component.</strong> A component without a
        docs page is not done. A docs page without a component is a lie.</li>
    <li><strong>The docs site is built with Flint.</strong> Docs needs
        (breadcrumbs, callouts, code blocks, sidebar) become real component
        requirements, not guesses.</li>
    <li><strong>Zero dependencies, forever.</strong> No build step for users;
        copy two files and go. Docs tooling must not leak into the library.</li>
    <li><strong>Flat, 1px borders, no shadows</strong> — the Material 2019–2020
        look — is the design constraint that keeps the library small and
        coherent.</li>
    <li><strong>Distribution is copy-paste</strong> (the shadcn model): the
        docs' core feature is a copy button on every snippet.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

